# Requirements — Statement review: every figure traced, the unclear lines first

Bet: statement-review, signed 2026-11-16. Scope is a showcase for one firm (D15, D24): a working model the underwriter can try, after which the firm's approver decides on a pilot (D14, D25). Forms and risk tags follow the template.

Revision 21, after D168 (changes requested under the owner's standing approval of 2026-11-19, after T12's twenty-eighth review, verify-80, and T03's twenty-seventh, verify-81; the owner had answered revision 20's question as D164). R4 and R42 change; their ids, forms and risk tags do not. R42 now says that each report a save's writer gets gives one answer, and that its causes, the words of any refusal or error it carries or is raised from, give no other. No part of a not-recorded report says that the save was recorded or is not confirmed. No part of a not-confirmed report says that the save was recorded, was not recorded or that nothing was written, and one whose take-back was not made names what stopped it in the save's own words and does not quote the take-back's refusal (D164, D168). This follows verify-80, in which a save whose take-back was refused because a case lock file was replaced quoted the lock check's refusal, 'nothing was written', and the not-recorded reports at the head rename and in a short write carried the same words in the error they were raised from. D168 speaks of a not-confirmed report; R42 says one answer for every report, as D164 does, and no not-recorded report at T12's 7fb3a23 says otherwise. R42 also says that whether the rename that publishes a save's head record was made is known from that rename, never inferred from reading the head record afterwards, so a head record that cannot be read in the re-check before its rename stops the rename, and the save answers not recorded (D168, after verify-80, in which such a save answered not confirmed). R4 now says that only the frozen v1 table as its bytes were verified is spared the exception check: a changed v1 names, after the changed-table refusal, each of its rules that carries an exception (D168, after verify-81, in which a copy of v1 that kept frozen: true and gained an unless was refused as changed with the unless unnamed). Beyond that check, R4 says, what else keeps a changed v1 from load